4. **ACCEPT is supported; I cannot justify a once-only announcement for the implemented read.**

   The ordinary read already has a concrete backing value and an assignment that returns it. The deletion lets that operation complete. Nothing in the inspected arm records a missing transition, acknowledges an interrupt, or requests an unsupported operation that would explain announcing it once.

