The draft preserves earlier D values when a later step fails and separates `BLOCKED` rows from `FAIL` rows without shrinking the denominator. Python syntax checks pass, and every proposed old-text anchor occurs once.

The anchor draft also installs the breakpoint before enabling IRQs in both legs. Bash validation could not start because the sandbox denied MSYS shared-memory initialization; emulator behavior remains unmeasured.
